# 🦅 Falcon OS

Developer : Aarav

Current Version : 1.04

Architecture : x86

Language : NASM Assembly

Current Mode : 16-bit Real Mode

------------------------------------------------------------

# Project Goal

Learn Operating System Development
from scratch.

Every version must teach
one new concept.

No blind copy-paste.

Understand everything.

------------------------------------------------------------

# Boot Process

Power Button
        │
        ▼
CPU Reset
        │
        ▼
BIOS Starts
        │
        ▼
BIOS checks boot device
        │
        ▼
Reads first 512 bytes
from disk
        │
        ▼
Copies bootloader to

0x7C00

        │
        ▼
CPU executes our code

boot.asm

------------------------------------------------------------

# Memory

BIOS loads us at

0x7C00

Therefore

[org 0x7C00]

is required.

------------------------------------------------------------

# CPU Mode

Current

16-bit Real Mode

Features

✔ BIOS Interrupts

✔ Direct Hardware Access

✔ Simple Memory

Limitations

❌ No Multitasking

❌ No Memory Protection

❌ No 32-bit Programs

❌ No GUI

------------------------------------------------------------

# Why 16-bit?

Because BIOS always starts
the CPU in Real Mode.

Every OS starts here.

Windows

Linux

FreeBSD

All begin in 16-bit mode.

------------------------------------------------------------

# Registers Learned

AX

General Register

AH

High 8 bits of AX

AL

Low 8 bits of AX

SI

Source Index

Used while printing strings.

SP

Stack Pointer

BP

Base Pointer

IP

Instruction Pointer

------------------------------------------------------------

# Instructions Learned

mov

Copy data

Example

mov ax,3

----------------------

cmp

Compare values

Example

cmp al,0

----------------------

je

Jump if Equal

----------------------

jmp

Unconditional Jump

----------------------

lodsb

Load byte

AL = [SI]

SI++

----------------------

int

Call BIOS

Example

int 10h

Video

int 16h

Keyboard

----------------------

cli

Disable interrupts

----------------------

hlt

Stop CPU

------------------------------------------------------------

# BIOS Interrupts

INT 10h

Video Services

Functions Used

AH = 0Eh

Print Character

AH = 00h

Video Mode

------------------------------------------------------------

INT 16h

Keyboard Services

AH = 00h

Wait for Key

Returns

AL

ASCII Character

AH

Scan Code

------------------------------------------------------------

# Keyboard Working

User presses key

↓

Keyboard Controller

↓

BIOS

↓

INT 16h

↓

AL contains ASCII

↓

INT 10h prints character

↓

Character appears on screen

------------------------------------------------------------

# Printing Strings

mov si,message

↓

lodsb

↓

AL gets character

↓

cmp al,0

↓

If zero

Stop

Else

↓

INT 10h

↓

Print Character

↓

Repeat

------------------------------------------------------------

# Boot Signature

dw 0xAA55

Required.

Without it

BIOS says

Not Bootable Device

